1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,742
Chapter nine — racks and the facility.

2
00:00:03,802 --> 00:00:14,465
This is where a design stops being a
diagram and becomes a purchase order.

3
00:00:14,525 --> 00:00:23,974
The Racks lens takes the services you
designed and puts them in real machines.

4
00:00:24,034 --> 00:00:37,556
IT load, heat, weight, inventory and
energy — across the top, always live.

5
00:00:37,616 --> 00:00:42,558
It can design the whole
estate from the architecture.

6
00:00:42,618 --> 00:00:54,659
Two data centres active-active, primary
plus DR, or a scale-up analytics build.

7
00:00:54,719 --> 00:01:10,161
Quick build does it deterministically.
Design facility hands it to Claude.

8
00:01:10,221 --> 00:01:20,665
It shows its working: nodes to chassis,
chassis to racks, racks to sites.

9
00:01:20,725 --> 00:01:33,345
Sites, racks, machines and
compute — counted, not estimated.

10
00:01:33,405 --> 00:01:40,351
And the estate lands on the canvas behind it.

11
00:01:40,411 --> 00:01:53,923
The rack elevation is the front face
— named services in real rack units.

12
00:01:53,983 --> 00:02:03,932
Turn it round: cable routing,
top-of-rack A and B, PDU channels.

13
00:02:03,992 --> 00:02:09,404
Back to the front.

14
00:02:09,464 --> 00:02:13,868
Then the hall itself.

15
00:02:13,928 --> 00:02:23,378
Rows, positions, and the
floor space they take.

16
00:02:23,438 --> 00:02:27,842
And the cabling.

17
00:02:27,902 --> 00:02:38,350
The pull list: every run, its
length, its type and its cost.

18
00:02:38,410 --> 00:02:47,860
Port headroom on each switch, and
what the whole plant costs to wire.

19
00:02:47,920 --> 00:02:51,531
Back to the elevation.

20
00:02:51,591 --> 00:03:01,038
On the right: core budgets, power
feeds in 2N, and hall budgets.

21
00:03:01,098 --> 00:03:12,046
Kilowatts, BTU per hour, kilograms per square
metre, floor area — against capacity, not vibes.

22
00:03:12,106 --> 00:03:16,852
Drawing set exports the lot as a document.

23
00:03:16,912 --> 00:03:22,057
Ask Larry is the facility
expert, on the same numbers.

24
00:03:22,117 --> 00:03:30,564
And the hardware catalog on the left
is what you are allowed to put in.

25
00:03:30,624 --> 00:03:34,070
From a sentence about a system —

26
00:03:34,130 --> 00:03:39,132
— to the racks it lands in.
